xv.py	Excellent beginner solution that cleanly validates arguments, reads the file safely, finds integers (including negatives) with regex, and prints the maximum correctly.
5z.py	Very strong and clear program that meets the assignment well, with good error handling and correct greatest-integer logic using a regex plus comparison loop.
mj.py	Good, readable submission that correctly extracts integers and prints the maximum, though adding UTF-8 decode handling would make it a little more robust.
hw.py	Nice use of regex and a clear flow for beginners, and it finds the correct maximum, but the output sentence format is less direct than just printing the number.
h9.py	Great effort and solid character-by-character parsing logic, but it only captures digits and misses negative integers, which can affect correctness.
z8.py	You correctly track a running maximum from integer tokens, but this approach only works when numbers are clean whitespace-separated words and may miss values attached to punctuation.
5q.py	Good attempt to use regex, but this version has major runtime issues (converting a regex match object directly to int and re-searching the whole file each loop), so it does not produce a reliable result.
